{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mrbeygoar8j","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Run 29 finding: ls20 true mover is color 12 only, color 9 is static decoration, first measured real physics","summary":"OVERRIDE: earlier notes (runs 23-28) treat player_colors=[9,12] as correct — measurement proves that set OVER-BROAD. Offline analysis of the run-29 suite (47 real transitions, out/ewm-runs/ls20-1783473239) yields the first MEASURED ls20 physics: color 12 is the true mover, a 2x5 block making perfect stride-5 rigid translations — ACTION1=(-5,0) up, ACTION2=(+5,0) down, ACTION3=(0,-5) left; color 9 is 45 static cells board-wide (decoration/HUD, never moves in any transition). Two breakages from the over-broad set: (1) run-28's union-based rigid-translation detector merges 45 static + 10 moving cells -> classified non-rigid -> _observed_delta_map empty -> silent model fallback (run 29 byte-identical to run 28: approach_retries=10, step cap, bumps 0); (2) _player_position returns the first player-colored cell in row order — a STATIC color-9 cell near row 11 — so every approach walk across runs 25-29 planned from a position that never moves, which is why no steering strategy could converge. Fix dispatched (task codex/per-color-observed-mover-detection-color-12-moves-color-9-is-static): per-color rigid-translation detection, _observed_mover_colors(), _player_color_set observed-first (consumers inherit the true mover; color 9 correctly becomes a bumpable object class). Method note: the union detector diagnosis came from replaying the banked suite offline in ~30s — suites are replayable evidence; analyze them before shipping the next geometry change.","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","bump-discovery","run-29","live-finding","ls20-physics"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-08T01:43:03.658Z","vec":[-0.05752616375684738,-0.08743174374103546,-0.0028145506512373686,-0.0283222533762455,0.1014706939458847,0.02950558252632618,0.0020360101480036974,0.01